Here is the build brief I'm working to:

**Concept — "Read the movement the way it is built."** The page is organised the way a movement actually is: energy through it, then material across it. Composition rule: a technical-drawing margin (index numerals + measured hairlines) down the left; content on a wide asymmetric grid. Type: Gambetta (display serif), Synonym (body), Tabular (all figures). Palette sampled from the materials — frosted German-silver paper, black-polish ink, blued-screw accent, one ruby jewel note for scarcity. Media: four real CC BY photographs of comparable movements and of bench work, captioned honestly as reference, not as Caliber 08.

```
Experience arc: orient (hero, plan view) → demonstrate (power path, live 5/s beat)
                → transform (four layers as an exploded 3.8mm caliper stack)
                → rest (specification) → prove (workshop, photographic ground)
                → decide (three finishes + reservation)
Signature component: the power path — six stages on one continuous torque line;
                selecting a stage traces energy from the mainspring up to it, and
                the escapement stage beats live at its stated 5 releases/second.
Post-hero peak: the layer stack — four bars scaled to true thickness, summing to
                the spec's 3.8mm, exploding on selection with a dimension line.
Continuity owner: the measured hairline — power spine, dimension line, spec rule,
                allocation mark; it carries a real value every time it appears.
Interaction baseline: one grammar route-wide — hairline darkens, ground lifts,
                index rule wipes; 160ms; blued focus ring; regional entrances.
Mobile: index gutter dissolves inline, power path becomes a tap-to-open vertical
                spine, stack rotates upright, finishes become radio rows.
```
